<?xml version="1.0"?>
<repository version="1.2"
            xmlns="http://www.gtk.org/introspection/core/1.0"
            xmlns:c="http://www.gtk.org/introspection/c/1.0"
            xmlns:glib="http://www.gtk.org/introspection/glib/1.0">
  <include name="GObject" version="2.0"/>
  <package name="documented-1.0"/>
  <namespace name="Documented"
             version="1.0"
             shared-library="libdocumented.so.0"
             c:identifier-prefixes="Documented"
             c:symbol-prefixes="documented">
    <enumeration name="Tone"
                 glib:type-name="DocumentedTone"
                 glib:get-type="documented_tone_get_type"
                 c:type="DocumentedTone">
      <doc xml:space="preserve">How loudly a note is read back.</doc>
      <member name="quiet" value="0" c:identifier="DOCUMENTED_TONE_QUIET">
        <doc xml:space="preserve">Read the note under the breath.</doc>
      </member>
      <member name="loud" value="1" c:identifier="DOCUMENTED_TONE_LOUD">
        <doc xml:space="preserve">Read the note out across the room.</doc>
      </member>
    </enumeration>
    <class name="Note"
           c:symbol-prefix="note"
           c:type="DocumentedNote"
           parent="GObject.Object"
           glib:type-name="DocumentedNote"
           glib:get-type="documented_note_get_type">
      <doc xml:space="preserve">Holds a short piece of text the user jotted down.</doc>
      <method name="copy" c:identifier="documented_note_copy">
        <doc xml:space="preserve">Copies the note text.

You must free the copy with g_free() when done.</doc>
        <return-value transfer-ownership="full">
          <doc xml:space="preserve">a copy of the note. Free it with g_free() when done.</doc>
          <type name="utf8" c:type="gchar*"/>
        </return-value>
        <parameters>
          <instance-parameter name="self" transfer-ownership="none">
            <type name="Note" c:type="DocumentedNote*"/>
          </instance-parameter>
          <parameter name="buffer" transfer-ownership="none">
            <doc xml:space="preserve">the buffer to copy into, which the caller must free with g_free()</doc>
            <type name="utf8" c:type="const gchar*"/>
          </parameter>
        </parameters>
      </method>
      <method name="list" c:identifier="documented_note_list">
        <doc xml:space="preserve">Lists the notes.</doc>
        <return-value transfer-ownership="full">
          <doc xml:space="preserve">a list of strvs. Free each item with g_strfreev() and free the outer list with g_free().</doc>
          <array zero-terminated="1" c:type="gchar**">
            <type name="utf8" c:type="gchar*"/>
          </array>
        </return-value>
        <parameters>
          <instance-parameter name="self" transfer-ownership="none">
            <type name="Note" c:type="DocumentedNote*"/>
          </instance-parameter>
        </parameters>
      </method>
      <method name="ownership_details" c:identifier="documented_note_ownership_details">
        <doc xml:space="preserve">Describes copied values.

The caller is responsible for freeing the list with g_strfreev() when it is no longer required.

Calling code is responsible for freeing the pointer with g_free() when it is no longer required.

The copy should be freed with documented_copy_free().

The contents should be freed with g_free() when no longer needed.

The returned contents must be freed with g_free().

The pointer must be freed with g_free().

That string needs to be freed by the callee using g_free().

The memory of the input has to be dynamically allocated and will eventually be freed with g_free().</doc>
        <return-value transfer-ownership="none">
          <type name="none" c:type="void"/>
        </return-value>
        <parameters>
          <instance-parameter name="self" transfer-ownership="none">
            <type name="Note" c:type="DocumentedNote*"/>
          </instance-parameter>
        </parameters>
      </method>
      <method name="allocator_details" c:identifier="documented_note_allocator_details">
        <doc xml:space="preserve">Describes allocator behavior.

In case a GCC compatible compiler is used, this function may be used automatically via g_free() if the allocated size is known at compile time.

Creates a new memory output stream, using g_realloc() and g_free() for memory allocation.</doc>
        <return-value transfer-ownership="none">
          <type name="none" c:type="void"/>
        </return-value>
        <parameters>
          <instance-parameter name="self" transfer-ownership="none">
            <type name="Note" c:type="DocumentedNote*"/>
          </instance-parameter>
        </parameters>
      </method>
      <method name="lifecycle_details" c:identifier="documented_note_lifecycle_details">
        <doc xml:space="preserve">Describes lifecycle details.

Note that filters run in another thread, so you cannot just free data the filter might be using. Instead, you should pass a #GDestroyNotify to documented_note_watch(), which will be called when the data is no longer needed.

In particular, if initialization fails with a `GError`, the only valid thing you can do with that note is to free it with g_object_unref().

The port is chosen by the system. This address, if requested, belongs to the caller and must be freed.

After calling this function, it is no longer possible to add more nodes. The only function that should be called after this is g_object_unref().

The items are not freed, so if the memory was dynamically allocated, it should be freed after calling this function.

The data contained in the resulting #GBytes is always zero-terminated. The resulting #GBytes should be
freed with g_bytes_unref() when no longer in use.

Buffers are recycled internally rather than handed to g_free().

Since you are providing a pre-allocated note buffer, you must also specify a way to free that data.

When the note is finalized, your destroy notification function will be called.</doc>
        <return-value transfer-ownership="full">
          <doc xml:space="preserve">a list of cell renderers. The list must be freed with g_list_free().</doc>
          <array zero-terminated="1" c:type="gchar**">
            <type name="utf8" c:type="gchar*"/>
          </array>
        </return-value>
        <parameters>
          <instance-parameter name="self" transfer-ownership="none">
            <type name="Note" c:type="DocumentedNote*"/>
          </instance-parameter>
        </parameters>
      </method>
      <method name="clause_details" c:identifier="documented_note_clause_details">
        <doc xml:space="preserve">Describes clause details.

Returns the label of the note, if any, which must be freed with g_free().

Reads the tooltip back, when set, into a buffer the caller must free with g_free().

Gets the icon of the note, if one was set, which must be unreffed with g_object_unref().

The buffer is reused, but if the note was detached, the caller must free it with g_free().

If the note holds a string, the location will contain a newly allocated string. Likewise if the note holds an array, the data should be freed using g_strfreev().

Reading a joined note returns a handle only if joining was requested. In that case, you must free this handle by calling g_object_unref().

The note takes ownership of the label.

On success, the returned note takes ownership of the descriptor. On failure, the caller must close the descriptor themselves.

Note that the note takes ownership of the filter if it is floating, so you have to ref and sink it if you want to keep a reference.

`DocumentedNote` objects are referenced by each reader, so once you have added all readers, you can drop the initial reference with g_object_unref().

The function takes ownership of the arguments, so you can write code like:

```c
note = documented_note_new (documented_label_new ("hello"));
```

Notes can be turned off in final releases of code by defining DOCUMENTED_DISABLE_NOTES, so code must not depend on any side effects from reading them.

To delete a note window, call [method@Gtk.Window.destroy].

You must use [method@GLib.Source.destroy] for sources added to a non-default main context.</doc>
        <return-value transfer-ownership="full">
          <doc xml:space="preserve">a newly created window; the note will take ownership of the returned value.</doc>
          <type name="utf8" c:type="gchar*"/>
        </return-value>
        <parameters>
          <instance-parameter name="self" transfer-ownership="none">
            <type name="Note" c:type="DocumentedNote*"/>
          </instance-parameter>
          <parameter name="label" transfer-ownership="full">
            <doc xml:space="preserve">the label text that the note takes ownership of</doc>
            <type name="utf8" c:type="gchar*"/>
          </parameter>
        </parameters>
      </method>
      <method name="read" c:identifier="documented_note_read">
        <doc xml:space="preserve">Reads the note back in the given tone.</doc>
        <return-value transfer-ownership="none">
          <type name="none" c:type="void"/>
        </return-value>
        <parameters>
          <instance-parameter name="self" transfer-ownership="none">
            <type name="Note" c:type="DocumentedNote*"/>
          </instance-parameter>
          <parameter name="tone" transfer-ownership="none">
            <doc xml:space="preserve">How loudly to read it.</doc>
            <type name="Tone" c:type="DocumentedTone"/>
          </parameter>
        </parameters>
      </method>
      <method name="search" c:identifier="documented_note_search">
        <doc xml:space="preserve">Searches the notes for a value.</doc>
        <return-value transfer-ownership="none">
          <type name="none" c:type="void"/>
        </return-value>
        <parameters>
          <instance-parameter name="self" transfer-ownership="none">
            <type name="Note" c:type="DocumentedNote*"/>
          </instance-parameter>
          <parameter name="value" transfer-ownership="none">
            <doc xml:space="preserve">free text to search for, for instance, "power"</doc>
            <type name="utf8" c:type="const gchar*"/>
          </parameter>
        </parameters>
      </method>
      <method name="shout" c:identifier="documented_note_shout" deprecated="1" deprecated-version="1.0">
        <doc xml:space="preserve">Reads the note back as loudly as possible.</doc>
        <doc-deprecated xml:space="preserve">Use read() with Tone.LOUD instead.</doc-deprecated>
        <return-value transfer-ownership="none">
          <type name="none" c:type="void"/>
        </return-value>
        <parameters>
          <instance-parameter name="self" transfer-ownership="none">
            <type name="Note" c:type="DocumentedNote*"/>
          </instance-parameter>
        </parameters>
      </method>
    </class>
  </namespace>
</repository>
